KZ3 patch 1069 (SPU pass 52, the quit-to-menu hang): unlifted code inside a WWS job's local-store range runs in the
full SPU interpreter, with the host call frames kept. KZ3's Amadeus mixer job (job_0127a180, wid 5 jm_amadeus) loads
a DSP plugin (job_0129bd80, linked for LS 0x8000 but lifted at 0x4000) for the level's stream voice and calls into it
through pointers (0x5E6C `bisl $0,$95` -> 0xB518, 0x6B1C -> 0x8030); the plugin calls back into the mixer's DMA helper
0x4D70 at its absolute address. Before: the indirect-branch miss went to the SMC microstep (a stub interpreter for
the job manager's generated save/restore code), and when the lifted helper returned (SPU_RET) into the plugin at
0xBA70 the drain bracket found no lifted code there and took the restart dispatch, which longjmps to the lane driver
and drops every host frame, including the policy module's job bracket: the lane's run ended inside the job
([pm-end] pc 0x4D70 lr 0xBAA8, status RUNNING), the job stayed claimed (job-list row slot 0 = 0, never done),
AmadeusScheduler's WaitForJobGroup 0x89D7C waited forever and the sound system's shutdown wait 0x300250 never
returned. Now: (1) spu_indirect_branch, for a policy-mode lane whose pc is in [0x4000, 0x3FE80) with code there and
no lifted function, runs spu_interp_run_until(pc, 0) (it stops at the first lifted address, the resident overlay
first, patch 1028) and dispatches from there; (2) spu_drain_call, when a bracket's inner loop ends at such an
unlifted pc, interprets until the bracket's return address or a lifted address and goes on, instead of the restart.
KZ3_SPU_WWS_INTERP=0 restores both old paths. [pm-end] marks: N:pc interpreter entered, J:pc where it stopped.
Upstream candidate (general: any title whose SPU jobs call runtime-loaded or differently-based code).

--- a/runtime/spu/spu_drain.c	2026-10-13 15:12:01.028934386 -0500
+++ b/runtime/spu/spu_drain.c	2026-10-13 15:12:01.043930284 -0500
@@ -518,6 +518,29 @@
                 continue;
             }
         }
+        /* KZ3 patch 1069: a lifted function returned (SPU_RET with this bracket live) into unlifted code inside a
+         * WWS job's LS range (the plugin that called it, see spu_indirect_branch). Interpret from there until the
+         * bracket's return address or a lifted address, keeping the host frames, instead of the restart dispatch
+         * below (which abandons every frame up to the lane's driver, and with them the PM's job bracket). */
+        {
+            extern int kz3_wws_interp_on(void);
+            const uint32_t p = ctx->pc & SPU_LS_MASK & ~3u;
+            if (ctx->policy_mode && kz3_wws_interp_on() && p >= 0x4000 && p < 0x3FE80 &&
+                (ctx->ls[p] | ctx->ls[p + 1] | ctx->ls[p + 2] | ctx->ls[p + 3])) {
+                extern uint32_t spu_interp_run_until(spu_context*, uint32_t, uint32_t);
+                spu_recent_mark(ctx, 10, p);
+                spu_interp_run_until(ctx, p, return_pc & SPU_LS_MASK);
+                spu_recent_mark(ctx, 11, ctx->pc);
+                if (ctx->status == SPU_STATUS_RUNNING) {
+                    if ((ctx->pc & SPU_LS_MASK) == (return_pc & SPU_LS_MASK)) {
+                        SPU_DRAIN_POP_IRQ();
+                        return;
+                    }
+                    g_spu_trampoline_fn = spu_indirect_branch;
+                    continue;
+                }
+            }
+        }
         {
             extern void spu_restart_dispatch(spu_context*);
             SPU_DRAIN_POP_IRQ();
